<title>UK: Buyout at UK software firm Policy Master.</title>
<headline>Buyout at UK software firm Policy Master.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The founder of Policy Master, a specialist British software house supplying the insurance industry, said on Tuesday he had regained control of the firm through a buyout from institutional investors General Accident Plc and Norwich Union.</p>
<p>In a statement Stephen Verrall said he had developed Policy Master into a company serving 1,000 clients among brokers and underwriters in 50 countries.</p>
<p>His management team was backed in the deal by venture capital group Gresham Trust, itself a unit of tobacco to financial services group B.A.T Industries Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
